From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max77705: battery health for the undocumented details

BAT_DTLS 0x06 is a battery overcurrent (stock's B2SOVRC; the MAX77818,
the same charger family, documents it so), and the driver called it an
unspecified failure. 0x07 is not documented; on the Galaxy Z Flip3 it
reads back with no input and a healthy battery (CHG_DTLS 0x8, BAT_OK
set), so the charger reported "Unspecified failure" whenever it was
unplugged. Report 0x06 as overcurrent and take BAT_OK for anything
undocumented.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c |   20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)


diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
index 54e147e..92e7f61 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
@@ -412,11 +412,25 @@ static int max77705_get_battery_health(struct max77705_charger_data *chg,
 		dev_dbg(chg->dev, "%s: battery ovp\n", __func__);
 		*value = POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_OVERVOLTAGE;
 		break;
-	default:
-		dev_dbg(chg->dev, "%s: battery unknown\n", __func__);
-		*value = POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_UNSPEC_FAILURE;
+	case MAX77705_BATTERY_RESERVED:
+		/* 0x06: battery overcurrent (stock's B2SOVRC; MAX77818 datasheet) */
+		*value = POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_OVERCURRENT;
+		break;
+	default: {
+		unsigned int int_ok;
+
+		/*
+		 * 0x07 is not documented and reads back with no input and a
+		 * healthy battery; take the chip's own battery-OK flag then.
+		 */
+		if (!regmap_read(regmap, MAX77705_CHG_REG_INT_OK, &int_ok) &&
+		    (int_ok & MAX77705_BAT_OK))
+			*value = POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_GOOD;
+		else
+			*value = POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_UNSPEC_FAILURE;
 		break;
 	}
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
